<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Integration Target</td><td>Philips IntelliVue MX750/MX850 patient monitors</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Protocols</td><td>HL7 FHIR R4 + IHE ITI-TF (ATNA, PIXV3)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Use Case</td><td>Email notification filtering for clinical alarm routing</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Hospitals</td><td>22 academic medical centers (Netherlands, Germany, Belgium)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Pre-assessment</td><td style="color:#0a0"><b>✓ PASSED (October 15, 2026)</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Clinical Safety Review</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>PENDING — Documentation required</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Review Deadline</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>November 18, 2026 (14 days)</b></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>二、What the Clinical Safety Review Covers</h3>
<p>Your gateway filters email notifications that carry clinical alarm routing instructions between Philips monitoring systems and hospital email systems. The Clinical Engineering Board must verify that your filtering algorithm:</p>
<ol>
<li><b>Never blocks or delays clinical alarm notifications</b> (false negative risk: patient harm)</li>
<li><b>Correctly identifies phishing attempts</b> that impersonate clinical systems</li>
<li><b>Maintains audit trails</b> compliant with IHE ATNA profile</li>
<li><b>Preserves PHI confidentiality</b> during filtering (HIPAA/GDPR compliance)</li>
<li><b>Handles HL7 FHIR resource formatting</b> in email bodies without data loss</li>
</ol>

<h3>三、Required Documentation</h3>
<table cellpadding=5 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Document</th><th>Details</th><th>Priority</th></tr>
<tr><td>Filtering algorithm specification</td><td>Complete logic flow, decision trees, scoring weights</td><td style="color:#e00">Critical</td></tr>
<tr><td>Clinical safe-list rules</td><td>How clinical alarm emails are prioritized</td><td style="color:#e00">Critical</td></tr>
<tr><td>False positive/negative test results</td><td>Clinical scenario validation data</td><td>High</td></tr>
<tr><td>PHI handling documentation</td><td>Data flow, encryption, retention, GDPR compliance</td><td>High</td></tr>
<tr><td>HL7 FHIR parsing validation</td><td>Test results for FHIR resource handling</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
<tr><td>Interoperability test logs</td><td>Integration test results with IntelliVue</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
</table>

