<h3>About Philips Certification Portal Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the submit button, you will be redirected to <b>accounts.philips.com</b> (Philips' official identity portal):</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your Philips Partner Account (or create one using your corporate email)</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, profile, offline_access)</li>
<li>Upload certification documentation</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we need your complete algorithm specification:</b> The Clinical Engineering Board (7 physicians + 3 clinical engineers) reviews your filtering algorithm to verify it cannot inadvertently block or delay clinical alarms. This is an EU Medical Device Regulation (MDR 2017/745) requirement for devices that interact with patient monitoring systems. Your algorithm specification includes decision logic, scoring weights, and clinical safe-list rules — all of which could cause patient harm if incorrectly configured. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-document upload (algorithm specifications + test data + compliance documentation = typically 100-200MB). This is standard for all MDR-required clinical safety reviews.
</p>

